{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_xeuonnwkv337owhyp5vpz45pmprieik4kys63aow6orvaluojuwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 6 tests pass. The build is clean — the warnings are just `dead_code` on test helpers in `src/bin/test_merkle_tree.rs` (which I am not allowed to modify) and a \"multiple build targets\" warning from `Cargo.toml` configuration that I shouldn't change either.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated both modules of the C project to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n**`src/blake2b.rs`** — A pure Rust BLAKE2b implementation matching the reference C version, using the `ckb-default-hash` personalization. Includes:\n- `blake2b_init`, `blake2b_init_key`, `blake2b_init_param`\n- `blake2b_update`, `blake2b_final`\n- Simple `blake2b` API\n- Internal compression function (`G`, `ROUND`) using `wrapping_add` and `rotate_right` for safety\n\n**`src/merkle_tree.rs`** — A complete pure-Rust port of the Complete Binary Merkle Tree (CBMT):\n- Buffer/queue/leaves/indices initializers\n- `cbmt_universal_swap`, `cbmt_simple_bubble_sort`, comparators\n- A ring-buffer queue (`cbmt_queue_*`) backed by a borrowed `&mut [u8]`\n- `cbmt_build_merkle_tree`, `cbmt_build_merkle_root` — bottom-up tree construction and root-only reduction\n- `cbmt_tree_build_proof` — produces `(indices, lemmas)` matching the C algorithm exactly (BFS over the queue, sibling-coalescing, and final ascending-by-node sort of indices)\n- `cbmt_proof_root`, `cbmt_proof_verify`, `cbmt_build_merkle_proof`\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!()`/`todo!()`/`panic!()` placeholders. All 6 tests pass under the 60-second timeout."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_read_input_tokens":60063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1236,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_u